summary:

In this post, I share how Grokbot won me over with its simplicity. I just chat with it, with no configs or settings in the way. I describe my setup, which includes a chief of staff bot, roughly twenty-five connected services, a personal email bot that checks mail at noon, and a bike repair bot that handles follow-ups. I also dispatch Cursor coding agents from my phone and get screenshot proof of the work. I do flag concerns about the changing economics of my sixty-dollar plan. Could simplicity and easy connections be the pattern that finally makes personal AI agents stick?
---
